            <ArticleTitle>Recent advances in managing hepatitis D.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1596</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12688/f1000research.11796.1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hepatitis D virus (HDV) infection leads to the most severe form of chronic viral hepatitis and requires the attention of a liver specialist. In this review, I will recapitulate recent advances in the management of HDV, present background information on HDV infection as well as current chronic hepatitis D treatment, briefly examine the HDV life cycle and discuss new management strategies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
